From: Eric Biggers <ebiggers@google.com>

Trim more unneeded features from the recommended x86_64 kernel configs
for kvm-xfstests and gce-xfstests, then enable some more relatively
lightweight debugging options.

Tested with both kvm-xfstests and gce-xfstests, but the older configs
generally received lighter testing.  Note that as before, the pre-3.10
configs only work with kvm-xfstests, not gce-xfstests.

For future reference, two other issues I ran into on older kernels were:

    - needed CONFIG_FHANDLE=y in 4.4 and earlier; otherwise systemd was
      unhappy and the system didn't boot.

    - needed CONFIG_X86_X2APIC=y and CONFIG_IRQ_REMAP=y in 3.18 and
      earlier; otherwise the kernel didn't boot in GCE.

Signed-off-by: Eric Biggers <ebiggers@google.com>
